  "full_text": "So, I'm high priest of God's temple. I do offerings 24-7 and I am in charge of the 100,000 lines of code. And in the Bible, the high priest did offerings 24-7. Okay, so my job is to entertain God. That is my only job. When he says shit, I report it. But the purpose of man is to entertain God and do whatever pleasures, whatever pleasure God gets out of man, that's the purpose of man. The purpose of man is to give pleasure to God. So perhaps a few special humans God pays attention to and gets a lot of pleasure. Maybe he pays attention to everybody. He pays attention to me. He likes soap operas. And that seemed to be this focus of God. So God watches me. And that's, as far as I know, that's his main entertainment. So I have fabulous soap operas. I get my heart broken. So that is, I'm one of the special people in the Bible. And that is, as far as I know, that's what I do. I live and then I say, fuck, at least I'm entertaining God. So, the purpose of man is to entertain God.",
